     <h1 class="title" title="Khandala Hill Station">Khandala</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/west-india-hill-stations/Khandala-hill-station.jpg" title="Khandala hill station" alt="Khandala hill station, hill stations in india, 

west india hill stations, Khandala" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> 96 kms from Mumbai, Maharashtra<br />
<b>Area:</b> 215 sq.kms<br />
<b>Significance: Jewel of the Sahyadri Mountains</b><br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 625m above sea level<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 30&#176;C - 35&#176;C, Winter 12&#176;C - 15&#176;C<br />
<b>Best time to visit:</b> October to May</p>     
<p><b>Khandala</b> is one of the most popular <b>hill stations in Maharashtra Sahyadri mountains</b> and is located 5 km from Lonavala, but another popular hill getaway. Located at an altitude of 625 feet, this quiet hill town is a weekend by the residents of <b>Mumbai</b> and <b>Pune</b>. rivers pleasant climate all year round, with the view of <b>Western Ghats, ancient caves</b> to explore, and <b>countless waterfalls</b> all add to the tourist attractions. This mountainous area offers numerous opportunities for camping and hiking and other activities outdoors.</p>








